This is actually a really easy fight, thanks in no small part to the Giant's unusually weak AoE attack, a magic neutralizer that can't actually do anything to stop the Sword of Ramias, and a critical hit that can always be blocked by Carver and neutralized by the Ghent Staff, Sage's Stone, and Hustle Dance.

So just have Lizzie alternate between Focus Strength + Attack/Defend/Ghent Staff (as needed), have Carver alternate between Knuckle Sandwich and Forbearance, have Terry spam Sage's Stone (switching armours as needed), and have Rex Oomph Carver before using Dance/Attack/Defend as appropriate.

== Gallows Moor ==

[[File:DQ6 Gallows Moor.png|thumb|right|You should have '''99''' Mini Medals and all '''16''' Dreamscapes by the end of this.]]

The mini-boss may be defeated, but this place is far from over.  Go down the stairs at point '''A''', across the electric floor, and talk to the NPC to get the Guards' Garb.  Put that on by using it from the item menu, loot the treasures you come across, go up to the 1st floor, talk to the guard between points '''F''' and '''H''', talk to the Captain guarding Blackmar at point '''P''', loot the three treasure chests on the 1st floor, then remove the Gaurd's Garb and talk to the woman running the bar.  Also be sure to snag the [[File:DQ3 SNES Book.png]] <span style="color:blue">16th Dreamscape</span> while you're there, if you're on the iOS/Android version.

Go talk to everyone you are told to talk to, and the guards will eventually try to execute someone!  This triggers a forced battle, but there's nothing you can do to win.  The Prison Guards are easy enough to beat, but Zozagel and Dogmus are unbeatable encounters.  Dogmus has 7000 HP, and will always paralyze your entire party on the 6th turn, even if you happen to have Kaclang up on that turn. And even if you do somehow kill him before the 6th Turn, the game will just ignore your victory.  You will be thrown in your cell, and the game will go on as if you lost.

{{Sidebar|title=If you wish to speed through this battle|float=left|width=505px|contents=This is the same situation as with Gardsbane Tower; you don't lose any Gold or anything if the Prison Guards beat you.  So if you really want to, you can have just one person in the active party after beating the Gallows Giant; then you can have them run inside the electric fields until they're at 1 HP.  Then Flee when you fight the Prison Guards wipe out her HP.  This is the fastest way of going through these fights.}}
{{-}}

== Waking Up ==

Observe the fallen guard once you wake up in your cell; the townsfolk will begin their riot and free you from your prison.  On your way to the 1st floor, Erdrick will give you 4x Seeds of Strength!  Use these on Carver, give your Staff of Antimagic to Lizzie (buy it from Swanstone or Sorceria if you don't have it), and have your party look like this:

Zozagel is collapsed right outside Blackmar's throne room.  He's immune to Sap, but relies on single-target physical attacks in a way that makes him even less of a threat than Terry; so feel free to beat him up if you like.  Whatever you do, get your gear in order and take on Blackmar!

