Blackmar starts off with two Dragooners on his side, who each have 336-420 HP.  In addition to that, he attacks twice per round, makes frequent use of AoE's, likes to use Kasap, and will also revive both of his minions to 100% HP if given the chance.  Given all these factors, he can be a huge step up in difficulty if one is not adequately prepared.

Fortunately, he has a critical vulnerability to Fizzle.  Land that on him with Lizzie, and there will be nothing he can do to stop you from spamming Kabuff and killing his minions.  And once you do that, and land two Saps on him, the match is basically over.  So the trick is surviving the first few rounds.

But, that shouldn't be too hard either.  The Sage's Stone does more than it's fair share of healing with Terry using it, and his armour switching allows him to adjust to the situation however he needs to.  So just have Terry spam the Sage's Stone, have Lizzie (or someone else) seal Blackmar's magic with the Staff of Anti-Magic, have Carver (or someone else) max out the party's Resilience with Kabuff, and have Rex use Oomph and Sap as needed (if you didn't need to replace him with a Kabuff user).  Once your party is set up, you can just have Carver Focus Strength + Double-Edged Slash spam Blackmar into oblivion as Lizzie and Rex pitch in their respective attacks.

== Aftermath ==

Go down the stairs at point '''A''' to talk to Benjamin again.  The next cutscene will trigger, and you will wake up the next day with a new mission.  Go talk to Benjamin once again, and he will give you the Orb of Truth.  Leave Gallows Moor, try to purchase the Yggdrasil Leaves you need if you haven't already, and head to the Prison of Sorrow.

